{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1522072-adventure-in-kaiserreich-what-if-the-the-central-powers-won-world-war-1","id":1522072,"title":"Adventure! in Kaiserreich, what if the the Central Powers won world war 1?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-04T14:32:16-07:00","id":1522072,"title":"Adventure! in Kaiserreich, what if the the Central Powers won world war 1?","content":"Hello Everyone,<br /> <br /> In the TC Eras discussion, we were also talking about alternative timelines and I wanted to share one of my favorites with you, Kaiserreich: Legacy of the Weltkrieg (<a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kaiserreich_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>). As the title suggests, in this world the central powers won World War 1. It started as a mod for the videogame hearts of iron, but it has evolved over the years and become a full-fledged setting that keeps growing. Seriously, I have nothing but praise for their creators and how they have managed to create a world that feels so real. Here's a quick summary from the wiki:<br /> <br /> <i>The Kaiserreich timeline departs from that of the &quot;original timeline&quot;, i.e. the real-world history during The First Weltkrieg in 1917, when the German Empire did not renew unrestricted submarine warfare, preventing the United States from joining the Entente. Later that year, the British naval blockade was partially lifted after a British submarine mistakenly torpedoed an American freighter heading to Germany, allowing the Central Powers to regain their energy. With renewed strength, the Central Powers launched several great offensives in Spring 1919, collapsing both France and Italy into revolutions. The Central Powers were declared the victors of the war in the Treaty of Versailles of 1918, triumphing over the Entente Powers. Germany became the dominant power in Europe, a position that it would carry into the world in the decade after.<br /> <br /> It is now 1936, and much has changed since the war's end. Revolutionary Syndicalism has overthrown the defeated Entente Powers, exiling the bitter royalists and creating a red alliance that seeks both revolutionary and revanchist expansion. The Whites emerged victorious from the Russian Civil War after a successful Ice March and Lenin's assassination, but iron-willed revanchism has since overtaken their new regime. The United States has become a hotbed of radical politics after years of neverending Great Depression, and there are whispers of armed paramilitaries making preparations for great uprisings that may collapse America into a Second American Civil War.<br /> <br /> Germany, still the preeminent power of the world, is facing challenges all around itself. Its influence stretches across Europe, Africa, and Asia, forming a seemingly impenetrable economic network that hides great ills beneath the surface. New alliances are forming as the old ones are dying, and all are preparing for a new global conflict. A Second Weltkrieg, promising to be several times bigger than the first, seems to lie on the horizon.</i>\u200b<br /> <br /> My intention with this thread is to try and imagine the Adventure! setting in this alternative timeline. How different would the characters and alliances be? Although I would like to do a short analysis of each character and alliance, there are a couple of general themes that would hange the game:<br /> <br /> The first one I mentioned in the TC eras discussion. The nations and political ideologies are more morally gray than in our timeline. What makes the setting so interesting to me is that without the pure evil of nazism and the extremism of the soviet union, democracy is not necessarily considered the facto &quot;good&quot; choice in this world (<a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/List_of_Political_Ideologies\" target=\"_blank\">Ideologies</a>). This doesn't mean there are no ideologies that are clearly more nefarious, but even then the ethical line is more blurry. This would make a character's political inclination much more important, especially for organizations that fight for the good of the world. I can easily imagine an AEON society struggling to reconcile not only the role of the inspired in the world, but also which political ideology should be supported. I think it could provide some great roleplaying opportunities.<br /> <br /> There are more, but while I work on them, I would love to hear your opinions on the subject. Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 09-05-2023, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T04:23:25-07:00","id":1522091,"title":"","content":"The AEON Society<br /> <br /> The ideals and objectives of the society remain the same for the most part. However, Maxwell knows that in just a few years the whole world is going to be engulfed in several wars with few safe places left in the world (one premise of the Kaiserreich setting is that the USA is going to go through a second civil war, and few countries will be able to remain outside one conflict or another). As such, the exploration of the world by the society has another secret objective set by Maxwell: to find and catalog places that will remain free from the wars.<br /> These places will work like secret bunkers filled with resources to help minimize the damage caused by the wars and help with the reconstruction efforts afterward. They will also be used to offer sanctuary to those escaping persecution for one reason or the other. However, these efforts have created a deep internal strife within the society for two reasons, the first one being that Maxwell hasn't been honest about the reason for their creation (he just says that they're chapter houses that will be useful in the future), the other being that members proclaim that those resources could better be spent trying to prevent conflicts in the first place.<br /> As the world becomes more unstable, so does the society, as its members push to be more active in world affairs and ditch their neutral position. They ask Maxwell how he can remain so passive while the war rages on every continent. He can't tell them, or he will alter the timeline too much. The situation degenerates even more as members start choosing sides due to different ideologies and loyalties. Maxwell refuses to change his position, and as such the society loses a lot of members.<br /> When the world is in flames, the AEON society is smaller, but much more focused and determined. The objective changes from one of exploration to one of damage control. On one hand, they use their charities and contacts to try and minimize the damage of the wars and promote peace, while on the other their teams do their best to make sure that the inspired, and especially old members, don't make the conflict worse with their abilities and super science.<br /> In conclusion, the aeon society of this world would be less an explorers society and more disaster relief and prevention. Also, due to political and national divides, the neutrality would push many members away from the society. The smaller society will struggle to achieve its objectives, but it will make it up with unity and focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 02-22-2024, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}